"thing explorer" is a notebook page
	<header level="1">
		ThingExplorer
		<header>The things a running program has made, live, with their properties and actions.</>
	</>

	<text class="lede" paragraph>The "Thing Explorer" tab of a runner's debug pane: every thing the running program has made, as a tree on the left, and the picked thing's properties and actions on the right. It changes as the program runs, so you can watch a todo get done, or a card move.</>
	<list class="spell-meta">
		<item icon="user">Written for: anyone changing the runners' debug pane, or reading its code</>
		<item icon="play">Live: a real <text code>&lt;spell-viewer&gt;</>, its debug pane opened on this tab</>
	</>

	<section label="1. Example">
		<icon slot="icon" name="eye"/>
		<text paragraph>The todos example, its debug pane open on "Thing Explorer": the pane under the app IS this component. Click a thing to see its details, then add a todo, or tick one, and watch the tree and the details change.</>
		<example "1. Example" description="The todos example, its debug pane on the Thing Explorer tab.">
			<html>
				<spell-viewer project="@spell/examples/TaskList" toolbar debug="things" height="760px"></spell-viewer>
			</html>
		</example>
		<text class="meta" paragraph>Live, from the app's element build, which this set's pages load: <text code>/element/spell.pack.js</>. <link target="src-packages-app" link="/src/app/">The app package</> builds it with <text code>yarn build:element</>.</>
	</>

	<section label="2. Using it">
		<icon slot="icon" name="code"/>
		<text paragraph>Each runner draws one in its debug pane, on the program's own copy of the spell runtime, once it's loaded:</>
		<text paragraph>SpellAppRunner.tsx · the Thing Explorer tab:</>
		<markdown>
			```typescript
			/** The Thing Explorer, once the runtime's loaded. */
			function things() {
			  return (
			    <Show when={loaded()} keyed>
			      {(copy) => (
			        <ThingExplorer
			          things={copy.runtime.core.things}
			          words={words()}
			          state={thingsState}
			          onStateChange={(state) => (thingsState = state)}
			        />
			      )}
			    </Show>
			  )
			}
			```
		</>
		<list bulleted>
			<item><text code>things</> is the list of things the running program made, from ITS copy of the runtime, never the page's own: each <text code>&lt;spell-viewer&gt;</> on a page has its own things.</>
			<item>The tree shows the program's top-level things first, then all of them: in the order they were made, under the heading whose code made them, or grouped by type. The buttons in its header switch.</>
			<item>Properties and actions read in spell's words, like <text code>draw (a todos-app)</>, when the project's words file is there; else by name.</>
			<item>An action that takes nothing has a play button, to do it now.</>
			<item>It's live, piece by piece: a changed property redraws just its own value, and a new thing adds just its row.</>
			<item><text code>state</> and <text code>onStateChange</> keep what's picked and open, so it comes back after a restart.</>
			<item>Its tree's rows are <link target="src-packages-app-docs-typeexplorer-html" link="/type-explorer">TreeRow</>s, and its headings <link target="src-packages-app-docs-scopedetailspane-html" link="/scope-details-pane">SectionMarker</>s, shared with the <link target="src-packages-app-docs-typeexplorer-html" link="/type-explorer">TypeExplorer</>.</>
		</>
	</>

	<section label="3. Props, and where it's drawn">
		<icon slot="icon" name="list check"/>
		<html>
			<ui-docs-api family="ThingExplorer"></>
		</>
		<text class="meta" paragraph>From its code, by <text code>yarn site:data</> in <link target="src-spell-app" link="/"><text code>spell-app</></>.</>
	</>

